course: dictionary
lesson: 330
title: Animated: made to move, or full of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one. «The animated film was full of talking animals.» Here animated means made from drawings, models or computer pictures shown quickly so they seem to move.
explain: «Mia was animated as she told us about her trip, waving her arms and grinning.» Now animated describes a person: lively, excited and full of energy. The clue is the waving arms and grinning, not a film at all.
explain: Animated is also the past form of the verb animate, which means to bring to life or make to move. Ask which meaning fits the sentence, then check it by putting your meaning in place of the word.
fact: Animated means made to seem to move, or lively and full of energy.
fact: An animated film is made from many drawings, models or computer pictures shown quickly.
fact: Animators make animated films frame by frame.
fact: Silent films came before about 1927, and King Kong in 1933 used a small gorilla model moved by hand.
fact: Toy Story, from 1995, was the first full-length computer-animated film, and Shrek followed in 2001.
exercise: «The animated film was full of talking animals.» What does animated mean here? | Brought to a stop | *Made from drawings or computer pictures shown quickly so they seem to move | Covered in paint | Sad and quiet
exercise: «Mia was animated as she told us about her trip.» What does animated describe? | The rain, which was heavy | The trip, which was boring | *Mia, who was lively and excited | The bus, which was late
exercise: «Toy Story, the first full-length computer-animated film, came out in 1995.» Which film was this? | Silent films | *Toy Story | Shrek | King Kong
test: Dad said Grandma's stories were so animated that we forgot the time. What does animated mean here? | *Lively and full of energy | Very old | Quiet and still | Made of drawings
test: To animate a flip book means to | *Make the pictures seem to move | Close the book and put it away | Read it aloud in a whisper | Tear out the pages
exam: Which of these is the past form of the verb animate? | animates | animator | animating | *animated
